-- title:
--   Isomorphic enhanced curves give kernel-ideal pairs differing by a unit
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, and let $X_0$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose points killed by $q'$ vanish. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ with $a<0$, $b<0$, and let $\theta$ be an injective ring homomorphism from [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring κ X₀`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32) — the subring of the additive endomorphism monoid of the points of $X_0$ generated by the set of additive maps that are either $0$ or given generically by rational functions in the coordinates, off a finite exceptional set — into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$. Let $W,W',W_1,W_1'$ be elliptic Weierstrass curves over $\kappa$, and let $\chi:X_0\to W$ and $\chi':X_0\to W'$ be nonzero additive maps lying in the corresponding sets of rational homomorphisms. Let $N\ne 0$ be a natural number with $N\ne 0$ in $\kappa$, and let $\psi:W\to W_1$, $\psi^{\vee}:W_1\to W$ and $\psi':W'\to W_1'$, $\psi'^{\vee}:W_1'\to W'$ be rational homomorphisms forming dual pairs, i.e. both composites of each pair equal $N$ times the identity, with $\#\ker\psi=\#\ker\psi'=N$. Assume further that $\varphi:W\to W'$ and $\varphi':W'\to W$ are mutually inverse rational homomorphisms and that $\varphi(\ker\psi)\subseteq\ker\psi'$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a unit $c$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ such that, writing $I(\alpha)$ for the kernel-ideal set of $\alpha$ (the set of elements of the rational endomorphism subring of $X_0$ of the form $\rho\circ\alpha$ with $\rho$ a rational homomorphism from the target of $\alpha$ back to $X_0$), one has $\theta(I(\chi'))=\theta(I(\chi))\,c$ and $\theta(I(\psi'\circ\chi'))=\theta(I(\psi\circ\chi))\,c$, the right-hand sides being the images of the two sets under right multiplication by $c$.
--
--   This is one direction of the dictionary, in Ribet's formulation, between enhanced supersingular elliptic curves with $\Gamma_0(N)$-type level structure over $\overline{\mathbb{F}}_{q'}$ and right ideal classes of an Eichler order in the definite quaternion algebra ramified at $q'$: an isomorphism of the pairs $(W,\ker\psi)\cong(W',\ker\psi')$ forces the two nested kernel-ideal pairs attached to $\chi$ and $\chi'$ to differ by right multiplication by one and the same unit. It feeds the equivalence [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_smul_eq_iff_exists_ker_eq_map_of_comp_eq_smul_id_of_card_ker_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_smul_eq_iff_exists_ker_eq_map_of_comp_eq_smul_id_of_card_ker_eq), which packages both directions.
